  "overview": {
    "text": "A square is a four-sided polygon with four equal sides and four right angles. It is distinctive because it belongs to several familiar quadrilateral families at once: it is both a rectangle, with four right angles, and a rhombus, with four equal sides; it is also a parallelogram and a regular polygon. This makes it a useful geometric model: its equal sides and right angles connect ideas about length, area, and perimeter in a particularly simple shape. If a side has length s, its area is s² and its perimeter is 4s. Its diagonals also have predictable relationships that help describe or calculate its dimensions.",
    "source_urls": [
      "https://www.mathsisfun.com/geometry/square.html",
      "https://openstax.org/books/contemporary-mathematics/pages/10-4-polygons-perimeter-and-circumference",
      "https://www.mathopenref.com/square.html"
    ]
  },
  "key_facts": [
    {
      "text": "A square is simultaneously a rectangle, a rhombus, a parallelogram, and a regular polygon.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.mathsisfun.com/geometry/square.html"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For side length s, the perimeter is 4s and the area is s².",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.mathopenref.com/square.html"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The two diagonals are equal; each bisects the other, and they meet at right angles.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.mathopenref.com/square.html",
        "https://www.mathsisfun.com/geometry/square.html"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A square’s diagonal has length s√2 when its side length is s.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.mathsisfun.com/geometry/square.html"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A square is a regular quadrilateral: all four sides are equal and all four angles are equal.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://openstax.org/books/contemporary-mathematics/pages/10-4-polygons-perimeter-and-circumference",
        "https://www.mathopenref.com/square.html"
      ]
    }
